    "created_at": "2021-08-18T21:29:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-08-18T21:32:46Z",
    "body": "The way that Starship handles module toggling is by deserializing the entire configuration file, changing the `disabled` line of the given module to the opposite of its current value, and then subsequently reserializing the config file. Unfortunately, when deserializing/serializing, comments don't get parsed.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, the Serde devs don't seem to want to support the parsing of comments ([see this issue](https://github.com/serde-rs/serde/issues/1430)). It may be worth looking into a different way of handling the toggle feature, as it seems like there won't be a terribly easy way to parse/keep comments with the current implementation.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
