    "created_at": "2021-09-13T23:15:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-13T23:15:36Z",
    "body": "From a purely API standpoint, is this an issue with serde or toml? It looks to me like we only directly depend on code from toml (though it's possible that toml implements this by providing custom serializers for TOML types).\r\n\r\nIf the issue is with toml and not serde, then we *might* be able to switch to another dependency. I caught a post today announcing the 0.3 release of [toml-edit](https://www.reddit.com/r/rust/comments/pno9mj/toml_edit_v03/). The crate itself is still fairly young, but it looks like it's used by `cargo-edit` in order to modify `Cargo.toml` files, so it seems that it's already used in at least one big project. I don't know if toml-edit is fast enough, and I don't know if it contains all the functionality we'd otherwise need (this would require an audit, I think).\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
