    "created_at": "2021-09-15T05:27:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-15T05:28:16Z",
    "body": "I've created a branch on my repo that replaces `toml` with `toml_edit::easy` (the almost drop-in replacement and the one that was identified as being more than 2x slower).\r\n\r\nWith a config file filled from one of the presets, I see about 0.2ms slower for prompt draws in a simple C/python repo and about 0.7ms slower for a toggle command. Are there other tests where we might be able to stress the parser more?\r\n\r\n```\r\ntoml_edit prompt draw:\r\n\r\nBenchmark #1: ~/tmp/starship-compare/starship-tomledit prompt -d 10s -j 3 -P /path/to/project --status 0 --pipestatus 0 0 0\r\n  Time (mean ± σ):       5.7 ms ±   0.3 ms    [User: 7.0 ms, System: 5.7 ms]\r\n  Range (min … max):     5.2 ms …   8.8 ms    309 runs\r\n\r\ntoml-rs prompt draw:\r\n\r\nBenchmark #1: ~/tmp/starship-compare/starship-tomlrs prompt -d 10s -j 3 -P /path/to/project --status 0 --pipestatus 0 0 0\r\n  Time (mean ± σ):       5.5 ms ±   0.3 ms    [User: 7.0 ms, System: 5.3 ms]\r\n  Range (min … max):     5.1 ms …   9.4 ms    292 runs\r\n\r\ntoml_edit toggle:\r\n\r\nBenchmark #1: ~/tmp/starship-compare/starship-tomledit toggle scala\r\n  Time (mean ± σ):       2.8 ms ±   0.2 ms    [User: 1.9 ms, System: 1.0 ms]\r\n  Range (min … max):     1.9 ms …   4.0 ms    723 runs\r\n\r\ntoml-rs toggle:\r\n\r\nBenchmark #1: ~/tmp/starship-compare/starship-tomlrs toggle scala\r\n  Time (mean ± σ):       2.2 ms ±   0.4 ms    [User: 1.5 ms, System: 0.8 ms]\r\n  Range (min … max):     1.1 ms …   4.9 ms    814 runs\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf anyone would like to clone the branch and run their own tests, it's available at https://github.com/chipbuster/starship/tree/toml-edit",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
