    "updated_at": "2021-10-05T17:26:20Z",
    "body": "Another thought: is it possible to use the toml parsing for when we just need to read structured data, but then use toml-edit when we want to make changes to the config file?\r\n\r\nThis might require reading config files twice when the user requests an edit, but in that case we're already okay with slightly reduced performance, and I don't think re-parsing should really take longer than a handful of milliseconds in any case.",
