    "body": "> Another thought: is it possible to use the toml parsing for when we just need to read structured data, but then use toml-edit when we want to make changes to the config file?\r\n>\r\n> This might require reading config files twice when the user requests an edit, but in that case we're already okay with slightly reduced performance, and I don't think re-parsing should really take longer than a handful of milliseconds in any case.\r\n\r\nI think the commands for editing are fairly separate from the structured TOML processing, so this should be possible. And if the config file needs to be changed elsewhere, it would likely need to be re-read anyway because the `easy` API is not format preserving.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, using `toml_edit` would avoid putting two separate TOML parsers in starship. But at least both `toml_edit` and `toml` are following the same TOML spec version now.",
